---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="Privacy Policy - Savants">
<style>
  .legal { max-width: 720px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 120px 24px 80px; }
  .legal h1 { font-size: 2rem; font-weight: 800; letter-spacing: -0.03em; margin-bottom: 8px; }
  .legal .updated { color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.85rem; margin-bottom: 48px; }
  .legal h2 { font-size: 1.2rem; font-weight: 700; margin-top: 40px; margin-bottom: 12px; }
  .legal p, .legal li { color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.95rem; line-height: 1.7; margin-bottom: 16px; }
  .legal ul { padding-left: 24px; }
  .legal a { color: var(--accent); text-decoration: none; }
</style>

<nav style="position:fixed;top:0;left:0;right:0;z-index:100;padding:18px 32px;backdrop-filter:blur(16px);background:rgba(10,10,10,0.92);border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);">
  <a href="/" style="font-weight:700;font-size:1.1rem;color:var(--fg);text-decoration:none;">savants</a>
</nav>

<div class="legal">
  <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
  <p class="updated">Last updated: April 29, 2026</p>

  <h2>What we collect</h2>
  <p>When you use Savants, we collect only what's necessary to provide the service:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Account information:</strong> Email address and name from Google or GitHub OAuth. Used for authentication and to contact you about your account.</li>
    <li><strong>Usage data:</strong> Which cloud tools you call, timestamps, and response times. Used for billing and to improve the service.</li>
    <li><strong>Payment information:</strong> Processed by Stripe. We never see or store your card number.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What we do NOT collect</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Your source code:</strong> Local tools (semantic search, file skeleton, callers, where_used) run entirely on your machine. Your code never leaves your device.</li>
    <li><strong>Telemetry:</strong> No analytics, no tracking pixels, no third-party scripts on the CLI.</li>
    <li><strong>Browsing data:</strong> We don't track you across websites.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Cloud tools</h2>
  <p>When you use cloud tools (diagnose_error, pr_risk, etc.), the query context (error messages, stack traces, diffs) is sent to our API for processing. This data is:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Processed in real-time and not stored after the response is returned</li>
    <li>Never used for training AI models</li>
    <li>Never shared with third parties</li>
    <li>Transmitted over TLS (HTTPS)</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Third-party integrations</h2>
  <p>When you connect Sentry, Slack, GitHub, or Jira, we store your API tokens encrypted at rest. These tokens are used only to fetch data you've authorized (events, messages, PRs) and can be revoked at any time by deleting the integration.</p>

  <h2>Data retention</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Account data: retained while your account is active</li>
    <li>Usage logs: retained for 90 days for billing</li>
    <li>Integration tokens: deleted immediately when you remove an integration</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>You can request deletion of your account and all associated data at any time by emailing <a href="mailto:hello@miguel.engineer">hello@miguel.engineer</a>.</p>

  <h2>Data location</h2>
  <p>Data is stored on Cloudflare's global network (D1 database, Workers KV). Cloudflare is SOC 2 Type II certified.</p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>Questions about privacy? Email <a href="mailto:hello@miguel.engineer">hello@miguel.engineer</a>.</p>
</div>
</Base>
